    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.snippets\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nWhen mini.snippets LSP server is active and the 'complete' option's 'o' flag is set, invoking completion raises this error:\n\n```\nE5108: Lua: Vim:E565: Not allowed to change text or change window\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'complete'\n        ...AD-47e3aec/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/completion.lua:539: in function 'callback'\n        ...AD-47e3aec/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/completion.lua:455: in function 'handler'\n        ...m/HEAD-47e3aec/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/client.lua:732: in function 'callback'\n        ...o/site/pack/core/opt/mini.snippets/lua/mini/snippets.lua:2652: in function 'request'\n        ...m/HEAD-47e3aec/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/client.lua:731: in function 'request'\n        ...AD-47e3aec/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/completion.lua:451: in function 'request'\n        ...AD-47e3aec/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/completion.lua:493: in function 'trigger'\n        ...AD-47e3aec/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/completion.lua:876: in function <...AD-47e3aec/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/completion.lua:866>\n```\n\nI initially saw this error a few days ago, after I switched to neovim nightly (from 0.11.whatever) and enabled 'autocomplete' and the 'complete' option's 'o' flag.\n\nAt first I saw the error only when editing gitcommit messages. At the time I did not see it while editing lua or go files.\n\nI temporarily removed mini.snippets from my config. Today (while making various other config edits), I restored mini.snippets, and saw the error while editing lua files.\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create a separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/'\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua' with this content:\n\n    ```lua\n    vim.o.autocomplete = true\n    vim.o.complete = 'o'\n    vim.pack.add({ 'https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.snippets'}, { })\n    require('mini.snippets').setup()\n    MiniSnippets.start_lsp_server()\n    ```\n\n3. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim`. Accept vim.pack's offer to install mini.snippets.\n\n4. Edit any file, including the init.lua file described above, and invoke completion by typing a character in insert mode.\n\nYou can also raise the error by typing Ctrl-N or Ctrl-P in insert mode. This gives the error even if `vim.o.autocomplete = false`.\n\n",
